---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
const questions = [{"prompt": "Wie viele Geschwister hat Claudia?", "options": ["zwei", "drei", "vier"], "answer": "drei", "why": "Claudia says: Ich habe drei Geschwister."}, {"prompt": "Wo wohnt Claudias Familie?", "options": ["In Österreich und Deutschland", "Nur in Ägypten", "Nur in Palästina"], "answer": "In Österreich und Deutschland", "why": "She describes family living in Austria and Germany."}, {"prompt": "Was bedeutet Nichten und Neffen?", "options": ["Children of a sibling", "Parents of a partner", "Grandparents"], "answer": "Children of a sibling", "why": "Nichten and Neffen are nieces and nephews."}, {"prompt": "Anna hat eigene Kinder.", "options": ["richtig", "falsch"], "answer": "falsch", "why": "Anna says: Ich selbst habe keine Kinder."}, {"prompt": "Annas Freunde sind ihre Familie.", "options": ["richtig", "falsch"], "answer": "richtig", "why": "Anna describes her friends as her constant family."}, {"prompt": "Wir ___ in Wien.", "options": ["wohne", "wohnt", "wohnen"], "answer": "wohnen", "why": "The wir form is wohnen."}, {"prompt": "Ihr ___ viele Freunde.", "options": ["haben", "habt", "hast"], "answer": "habt", "why": "The ihr form is habt."}, {"prompt": "Ich habe ___ Bruder.", "options": ["ein", "eine", "einen"], "answer": "einen", "why": "Bruder is masculine; the accusative form is einen Bruder."}];
---
<Base title="Lesson 3 extension: families and connections" description="Read about Claudia and Anna’s families, listen to Claudia, and practise German family vocabulary and grammar.">
<div class="lesson-two"><header class="lesson-hero"><div class="wrap">
<a class="back" href="/resources/german-async#e1">← Back to your learning path</a><p class="eyebrow">UNIT 01 · LESSON 03 · EXTENSION PRACTICE</p><h1>Families come<br /><em>in many forms.</em></h1><p class="intro">Meet Claudia and Anna. Explore how they describe the people in their lives.</p><p class="context">Follow-up practice for <span lang="de">Lektion 3: Familie</span>. Complete the <a href="/resources/german-lesson-3-main">main lesson</a> first, then explore these new readings and listening tasks.</p><nav aria-label="Lesson steps"><a href="#read">01 Read &amp; listen</a><a href="#watch">02 Watch</a><a href="#practice">03 Practise</a><a href="#write">04 Write</a></nav></div></header>
<div class="wrap lesson-body"><section id="read" aria-labelledby="read-title"><p class="eyebrow">01 / READ &amp; LISTEN</p><h2 id="read-title">Two ways to describe family.</h2><p>Read each account for its main idea first. Then look for who belongs to each family and where they live.</p><article class="reading"><h3>Claudia David</h3><p lang="de">Eine sehr interessante Familie habe ich. Meine Mutter ist Ägypterin und mein Vater ist Palästinenser—da fängt der Spaß an! Obwohl sie die gleiche Sprache haben, Arabisch, ist der Dialekt anders. Ich habe drei Geschwister. Sie sind alle verheiratet und ich habe viele Nichten und Neffen. Sie haben mich eine stolze Tante gemacht! Wir sind super divers—eine Mischung haben wir in unserer Familie. Es gibt Leute aus Österreich, es gibt Leute aus Syrien, aus Ägypten, und die Kinder sind teilweise in Österreich geboren, andere sind in Deutschland geboren. Wir haben deutsche Kinder und österreichische Kinder, auch von der Nationalität her. Ein Bruder von mir hat zwei Töchter, die eine ist Österreicherin, die andere ist Deutsche. Ein Teil von der Familie wohnt in Wien—in Österreich—und ein Teil wohnt in Deutschland.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="/assets/german/lesson3/claudia.mp4" aria-label="Claudia describes her family">Your browser does not support this audio player.</audio><a class="small" href="/assets/german/lesson3/claudia.mp4" download>Download Claudia’s audio</a></article>
<article class="reading"><img src="/assets/german/lesson3/anna.jpg" alt="Anna, whose family account appears below" loading="lazy" /><h3>Anna</h3><p lang="de">Ich selbst habe keine Kinder, aber ich habe sehr viele Freunde. Also meine Freunde sind meine konstante Familie. Einer meiner Ex-Freunde, mit dem ich 11 Jahre zusammen war, ist neu liiert, und mit seiner neuen Partnerin ist er 12 Jahre zusammen. Sie haben zusammen ein Kind. Die Tochter ist jetzt 11. Wir feiern immer gemeinsam Ostern und manchmal auch Weihnachten. Das ist auch eine Familie für mich. Wir sind befreundet und wir verstehen uns auch gut.</p><p class="small">Anna’s audio was not included in the supplied files. Use the reading for the questions below.</p></article></section>
<section id="watch" aria-labelledby="watch-title"><p class="eyebrow">02 / LISTENING PRACTICE</p><h2 id="watch-title">Listen for family connections.</h2><p>Watch the video, note any family words you recognise, then replay to check. Write down one phrase you would like to use yourself.</p><div class="video"><iframe title="Lesson 3 family listening activity" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/288166917?h=cc4562d81b" width="640" height="360" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe></div><p class="small">The video requires internet. <a href="https://player.vimeo.com/video/288166917?h=cc4562d81b">Open it separately</a> if the player does not load.</p></section>
<section id="practice" aria-labelledby="practice-title"><p class="eyebrow">03 / CHECK &amp; APPLY</p><h2 id="practice-title">People, verbs and connections.</h2><p class="tip">Need a reminder? Review <a href="/resources/german-lesson-3-main#practice">pronouns, verb forms and direct objects in the main lesson</a>, then return here for practice.</p><p>Answer from the readings and what you learned in the main lesson. Check your answers, read the feedback, and try again.</p>
 <form id="lesson-quiz">{questions.map((q,i)=><fieldset data-answer={q.answer} data-explanation={q.why}><legend><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span> <span lang="de">{q.prompt}</span></legend><div class="choices">{q.options.map(option=><label><input type="radio" name={`q${i}`} value={option}/><span lang="de">{option}</span></label>)}</div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>)}<div class="quiz-actions"><button type="submit">Check my answers</button><button type="reset" class="secondary">Try again</button></div><p id="quiz-score" role="status"></p></form>
 <noscript><p>Interactive checking needs JavaScript. Answer key: {questions.map((q,i)=>`${i+1}. ${q.answer}`).join(' · ')}.</p></noscript>
</section><section id="write" aria-labelledby="write-title"><p class="eyebrow">04 / MAKE IT YOURS</p><h2 id="write-title">Describe a family.</h2><ol class="speaking"><li>Write two sentences about Claudia’s or Anna’s family using <span lang="de">haben</span> and <span lang="de">wohnen</span>.</li><li>Describe your own family, chosen family, or an invented family in four sentences. Mention people, connections and where they live.</li><li>Underline your verbs and check that they match the subject. Check <span lang="de">ein / eine / einen</span> after <span lang="de">haben</span>.</li></ol><p class="example" lang="de">Wir wohnen in Berlin. Ich habe einen Bruder und eine Schwester.</p><p>Useful words: <span lang="de">die Eltern</span> (parents), <span lang="de">die Geschwister</span> (siblings), <span lang="de">die Großeltern</span> (grandparents), <span lang="de">die Nichte</span> (niece), <span lang="de">der Neffe</span> (nephew), <span lang="de">befreundet</span> (friends with one another), <span lang="de">verheiratet</span> (married).</p><a class="next" href="/resources/german-async#e1">Return to the curriculum →</a></section>
<aside class="source"><h2>Source &amp; adaptation</h2><p>Adapted from <a href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/e1/l3/erw/">Grenzenlos Deutsch, Lektion 3: Erweiterung</a>, supplied as a saved-page archive, under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Reading texts and Anna’s image are reproduced from the archive; Claudia’s audio was supplied separately. Grammar explanations and writing tasks are condensed and adapted. Eight text-based questions replace the original embedded exercises; they are not a complete reproduction of those activities. The Vimeo video remains subject to its owner’s rights. This page has no offline-saving feature.</p><p>Original funding: National Endowment for the Humanities and the Mansergh-Stuessy Fund for College Innovation. Ramzunā Languages is not affiliated with the original authors.</p></aside></div></div></Base>
<script>
const quiz = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#lesson-quiz');
quiz?.addEventListener('submit',event=>{event.preventDefault();let score=0;const fields=quiz.querySelectorAll<HTMLFieldSetElement>('fieldset');fields.forEach(field=>{const selected=field.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input:checked');const correct=selected?.value===field.dataset.answer;if(correct)score++;const feedback=field.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.feedback')!;feedback.textContent=!selected?'Choose an answer first.':`${correct?'Correct.':'Not quite.'} ${field.dataset.explanation}`;field.dataset.result=!selected?'empty':correct?'correct':'incorrect';});document.querySelector('#quiz-score')!.textContent=`${score} of ${fields.length} correct. Review the feedback above and try again whenever you like.`;});
quiz?.addEventListener('reset',()=>{quiz.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.feedback').forEach(el=>el.textContent='');quiz.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('fieldset').forEach(el=>delete el.dataset.result);document.querySelector('#quiz-score')!.textContent='';});
</script>
